{"abstract":"We present an approach to the proactive enforcement of provisions and obligations, suitable for building policy enforcement mechanisms that both prevent and cause system actions. Our approach encompasses abstract requirements for proactive policy enforcement, a system model describing how enforcement mechanisms interact with and control target systems, and concrete policy languages and associated enforcement mechanisms. As examples of policy languages, we consider finite automata and timed dynamic condition response (DCR) graphs. We use finite automata to illustrate the basic principles and DCR graphs to show how these principles can be adapted to a practical, real-time policy language. In both cases, we show how to algorithmically determine whether a given policy is enforceable and, when this is the case, construct an associated enforcement mechanism. Our approach improves upon existing formalisms in two ways: (1) we exploit the target system's existing functionality to avert policy violations proactively, rather than compensate for them reactively; and (2) rather than requiring the manual specification of remedial actions in the policy, we deduce required actions directly from the policy.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Basin, David","Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749105"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich"],"keyword":["Access control","Business process modeling","Obligations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proactive enforcement of provisions and obligations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-749105","identifier":[{"id":"85196660902","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c6918be5-bde2-4b50-8876-1f3e2afb5ccb"],"keyword":["Access control","business process modeling","obligations","run-time enforcement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-98E72C012B118C306E2E0F03DA4354BE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"David","key":"basinpau","last":"Basin","name":"Basin, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3233/jcs-210078","issn":["0926227X","18758924"],"issn_org":["0926227X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Computer Security","pages":"247-289","status":"p","title":"Journal of Computer Security","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196660902"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c6918be5-bde2-4b50-8876-1f3e2afb5ccb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Proactive enforcement of provisions and obligations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-749105","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Most contemporary process discovery methods take as inputs only positive examples of process executions, and so they are one-class classification algorithms. However, we have found negative examples to also be available in industry, hence we build on earlier work that treats process discovery as a binary classification problem. This approach opens the door to many well-established methods and metrics from machine learning, in particular to improve the distinction between what should and should not be allowed by the output model. Concretely, we (1) present a verified formalisation of process discovery as a binary classification problem; (2) provide cases with negative examples from industry, including real-life logs; (3) propose the Rejection Miner binary classification procedure, applicable to any process notation that has a suitable syntactic composition operator; (4) implement two concrete binary miners, one outputting Declare patterns, the other Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs; and (5) apply these miners to real world and synthetic logs obtained from our industry partners and the process discovery contest, showing increased output model quality in terms of accuracy and model size.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Slaats, Tijs","Debois, Søren","Back, Christoffer Olling","Christfort, Axel Kjeld Fjelrad"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721092"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Namibia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Servicenow Denmark ApS (Biz)"],"keyword":["Binary classification","Dynamic Condition Response Graphs","Labelled event logs","Negative examples","Process mining"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"foundations and practice of binary process discovery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.is.2023.102339","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721092","identifier":[{"id":"85183743346","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8ef851e7-d6e3-4bcf-b7eb-9b6ac5fc4255"],"keyword":["Binary classification","DisCoveR","Dynamic condition response graphs","Labelled event logs","Negative examples","Process mining"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8241E1CC7D3EF916D0383AF4948F41F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/382758441/Foundations_and_practice.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.is.2023.102339","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["DCR Solutions A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"na","key":"servicenow denmark aps","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Servicenow Denmark ApS (Biz)","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Christoffer Olling","key":"backpau","last":"Back","locid":"0ce144c3-eaf9-43e2-8f2b-03d6e4212b6a","name":"Back, Christoffer Olling","orcid":"0000-0001-7998-7167","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Axel Kjeld Fjelrad","key":"christfortpau","last":"Christfort","locid":"93296adf-650b-45c5-99fe-13923420b0f5","name":"Christfort, Axel Kjeld Fjelrad","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.is.2023.102339","issn":["03064379","18736076"],"issn_org":["03064379"],"journal":"Information Systems","paperid":"102339","status":"p","title":"Information Systems","volume":"121"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183743346"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","dcr solutions a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8ef851e7-d6e3-4bcf-b7eb-9b6ac5fc4255"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Foundations and practice of binary process discovery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721092","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We provide a practical translation from the Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) process modelling language to the Transaction Execution Approval Language (TEAL) used by the Algorand blockchain. Compared to earlier implementations of business process notations on blockchains, particularly Ethereum, the present implementation is four orders of magnitude cheaper. This translation has the following immediate ramifications: (1) It allows decentralised execution of DCR-specified business processes in the absence of expensive intermediaries (lawyers, brokers) or counterparty risk. (2) It provides a possibly helpful high-level language for implementing business processes on Algorand. (3) It demonstrates that despite the strict limitations on Algorand smart contracts, they are powerful enough to encode models of a modern process notation.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Xu, Yibin","Slaats, Tijs","Düdder, Boris","Debois, Søren","Wu, Haiqin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747551"],"event":{"end":"2022-05-06","place":"Saint George, gd","start":"2022-05-02","title":"26th International Conference on Financial Cryptography and Data Security, FC 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Inter institutional collaboration","Smart contracts"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distributed and adversarial resistant workflow execution on the algorand blockchain","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-32415-4_35","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747551","identifier":[{"id":"85172673938","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-19e78cfa-5a4f-4427-9694-e5c8e0fd4f20"],"keyword":["Algorand","Applications of blockchain","Inter-institutional collaboration","Smart contracts"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BCEF9DC6DB392BD7DF5AAD8BAAC6C6A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/394342358/Distributed_and_Adversarial_Resistant.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-32415-4_35","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yibin","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"08a435ed-3aab-4eec-88f1-c4e8c74b7155","name":"Xu, Yibin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Boris","key":"düdderpau","last":"Düdder","locid":"26641b70-8c76-4150-ae85-086cfa904763","name":"Düdder, Boris","orcid":"0000-0002-0241-7729","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Haiqin","k