{"abstract":"This paper addresses the open technical problems of evolving executable, event-based process models by refinement, that is, by iteratively expanding a model until it has the required level of detail. Such iterative development is helpful because of the expectation that the next-step model is semantically compatible with the previous one, only with more detail. We provide in this paper a formal notion of refinement of single atomic actions (events) into entire subprocesses, and a theoretical framework for providing guarantees that such a next-step model is formally a refinement of the previous one. Our work is set within the declarative, event-based process modelling language of timed Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs, which can express timed constraints (conditions with delay and obligations with deadlines) between events, liveness, safety, and concurrency. Concretely, we extend DCR graph syntax and semantics with a notion of subprocess, provide examples of its use, and give sound approximations of situations where replacing an event with a subprocess formally is a refinement of the original process.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Normann, Håkon","Debois, Søren","Slaats, Tijs","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-529118"],"event":{"acronym":"BPM","end":"2021-09-10","place":"Rome, it","start":"2021-09-06","title":"19th International Conference on Business Process Management, BPM 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Action refinement","DCR Graphs","Decomposition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"zoom and enhance action refinement via subprocesses in timed declarative processes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-529118","identifier":[{"id":"85115199701","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e334f24b-668f-478d-9c20-53a84b03e9bd"],"keyword":["Action refinement","DCR graphs","Decomposition","Subprocesses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-60A646DD3C83DBD4806F89316EE85542"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["DCR Solutions A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Håkon","key":"normannpau","last":"Normann","locid":"68370c00-7aca-4a84-97cd-509727ec4a96","name":"Normann, Håkon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Artem","key":"polyvyanyypedh","last":"Polyvyanyy","name":"Polyvyanyy, Artem","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Moe Thandar","key":"wynnpedh","last":"Wynn","name":"Wynn, Moe Thandar","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Amy","key":"vanlooypedh","last":"Van Looy","name":"Van Looy, Amy","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manfred","key":"reichertpedh","last":"Reichert","name":"Reichert, Manfred","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-85469-0_12","isbn":["9783030854683"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"161-178","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Business Process Management - 19th International Conference, BPM 2021, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115199701"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","dcr solutions a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e334f24b-668f-478d-9c20-53a84b03e9bd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Zoom and Enhance : Action Refinement via Subprocesses in Timed Declarative Processes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-529118","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Business processes, data, and run-time control state are all key elements in the design of enterprise applications. However, the different layers for processes, data, and control are usually represented using different technologies that must be explicitly combined and kept in sync. We introduce ReGraDa, a process definition and programming language inspired by the declarative business process language Dynamic Condition Response Graphs and targeting the integrated description of business processes, data and run-time state as reactive graph data. ReGraDa processes compile directly to a data-centric graph-based system (neo4j/cypher), allowing for the database system to manage a process without the need for an external execution engine. The underlying graph structure allows for the definition of native data relations between data elements that subsumes the integrity guaranties of relational and the semi-structured data models. Graph relationships are also used to represent data-dependency and control-flow in the database. We present the reactive semantics of the language, a translation from ReGraDa to cypher, evaluate its performance, and briefly discuss future work and applications.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Galrinho, Leandro","Seco, João Costa","Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Normann, Håkon","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518521"],"event":{"acronym":"COORDINATION","end":"2021-06-18","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2021-06-14","title":"23rd IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference on Coordination Models and Languages, COORDINATION 2021 held as part of 16th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NOVA Laboratory for Computer Science and Informatics","NOVA University Lisbon"],"le