ing","key":"backpau","last":"Back","locid":"0ce144c3-eaf9-43e2-8f2b-03d6e4212b6a","name":"Back, Christoffer Olling","orcid":"0000-0001-7998-7167","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"14","publisher":"Department of Computer Science, University of Copenhagen","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6226c8de-945f-44c8-9651-2ace663c284b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Imperative versus Declarative Process Mining : An Empirical Comparison","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-452152","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We study non-equivocation in synchronous agreement protocols: the restriction on faulty processes that they cannot act differently towards distinct non-faulty processes. Guarantees of non-equivocation have been used to provide improved fault tolerance in agreement protocols, and various mechanisms for achieving it have been proposed. However, the exact meaning of non-equivocation varies subtly in the literature. In this paper, we propose two different formal notions of non-equivocation: strong and weak. We define both as fault models for synchronous agreement protocols with reliable channels, and we show how the two models yield distinct bounds for the minimal number of communication rounds required and the maximum number of faulty processes tolerable to achieve agreement: 1 round, n > t for strong non-equivocation; and t + 1 rounds, n > 2t for weak non-equivocation. This makes weak non-equivocation the only fault model with a lower bound on fault tolerance of n > 2t for broadcast agreement and interactive consistency, confirming the folklore knowledge that equivocation is, in a sense, the most critical of the Byzantine faults. Finally, we show how the weak and strong non-equivocation fault models relate to well-known agreement problems: strong non-equivocation corresponds to Byzantine broadcast and weak non-equivocation to crusader agreement.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Madsen, Mads Frederik","Debois, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381798"],"event":{"acronym":"PODC","title":"ACM Symposium on Principles of Distributed Computing"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Byzantine faults","Fault tolerance","Formal fault models","Non equivocation","Synchronous agreement protocols"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the subject of non equivocation defining non equivocation in synchronous agreement systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu.dk/people/debois/papers/podc20.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381798","identifier":[{"id":"85090359320","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-239736e4-31f0-4b8d-8c93-7f6d44494a62"],"keyword":["Byzantine faults","Fault tolerance","Formal fault models","Non-equivocation","Synchronous agreement protocols"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-05A02B7B3AB256B8853D7543B38B30FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu.dk/people/debois/papers/podc20.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Frederik","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Mads Frederik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3382734.3405731","eisbn":["9781450375825"],"pages":"159-168","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"PODC '20: Proceedings of the 39th Symposium on Principles of Distributed Computing","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090359320"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-239736e4-31f0-4b8d-8c93-7f6d44494a62"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On the Subject of Non-Equivocation : Defining Non-Equivocation in Synchronous Agreement Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381798","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we take technical and practical steps towards the modularisation of compliant-by-design executable declarative process models. First, we demonstrate by example how the specific language of timed DCR graphs is capable of modelling complex legislation, with examples from laws regulating the functioning of local governments in Denmark. We then identify examples of law paragraphs that are beyond these modelling capabilities. This incompatibility arises from subtle and—from a computer science perspective—non-standard interactions between distinct paragraphs of the law, which must then become similar interactions between model fragments. To encompass these situations, we propose a notion of networksofprocesses, where the processes are allowed to interact and regulate their interaction through the novel mechanisms of exclusion and linking. Networks are parametric in the underlying process formalism, allowing interactions between processes specified in arbitrary and possibly distinct trace-language semantics formalisms as the individual models. Technically, we provide a sufficient condition for a good class of network compositions to realise refinement of the constituent processes. Finally, parts of the theoretical framework (networks and exclusion) have been implemented by our industry partners, and we report on a preliminary evaluation suggesting that inter-model synchronisation is indeed both necessary and helpful in practical modelling scenarios.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","López, Hugo A.","Slaats, Tijs","Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S02-081.48-033016"],"event":{"end":"2020-11-20","place":"Lugano, ch","start":"2020-11-16","title":"16th International Conference on Integrated Formal Methods - IFM 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Compliance by design","Dynamic Condition Response DCR Graphs","Faculty of Science","Law","Process modeling","Process modelling","Refinement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chain of events modular process models for the law","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.mendeley.com/catalogue/83330326-8e9a-35f9-80eb-7287fa480204/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-081.48-033016","identifier":[{"id":"85097370718","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-141af09a-ec23-4d38-8e26-a83d7b259937","ku-490db1fe-9da2-4905-b7b7-b5303d9c6034"],"keyword":["Compliance by design","Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs","Faculty of Science","Law","Laws and Regulations [DD500]","Process modeling","Process modelling","Refinement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0400C51CCC6AA316626DFA773DB85A88"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["DCR Solutions A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Software and Process Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Hugo A.","key":"lópezpau","last":"López","locid":"bb8c3de5-1755-46c4-a356-13eb16301a39","name":"López-Acosta, Hugo-Andrés","name_org":"López, Hugo A.","orcid":"0000-0001-5162-7936","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amine","key":"abbadandaloussipau","last":"Abbad Andaloussi","locid":"ec567f0e-aa1c-42e2-a523-fccf2f03efbe","name":"Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","orcid":"0000-0002-3404-7849","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-63461-2_20","eisbn":["9783030634612"],"isbn":["9783030634605"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"368-386","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Integrated Formal Methods: 16th International Conference, IFM 2020, Lugano, Switzerland, November 16–20, 2020, Proceedings","volume":"12546"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097370718"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","dcr solutions a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-141af09a-ec23-4d38-8e26-a83d7b259937","ku-490db1fe-9da2-4905-b7b7-b5303d9c6034"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Chain of Events: Modular Process Models for the Law","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.48-033016","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We report on a new approach to co-creating adaptive case management systems jointly with end-users, developed in the context of the Effective co-created and compliant adaptive case Management Systems for Knowledge Workers (EcoKnow.org) research project. The approach is based on knowledge from prior ethnographic field studies and research in the declarative Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) technology for model-driven design of case management systems. The approach was tested in an operational environment jointly with the danish municipality of Syddjurs by conducting a service-design project and implementing an open source case manager tool and a new highlighter tool for mapping between textual specifications and the DCR notation. The design method and technologies were evaluated by understandability studies with endusers. The study showed that the development could be done in just 6 months, and that the new highlighter tool in combination with the traditional design and simulation tools, supports domain experts formalise and provide traceability between their interpretations of textual specifications and the formal models.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas","Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","Christensen, Lars Rune","Debois, Søren","Healy, Nicklas Pape","López, Hugo A.","Marquard, Morten","Møller, Naja L. Holten","Petersen, Anette Chelina Møller","Slaats, Tijs","Weber, Barbara"],"cuid":["S02-082.74-037184"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSP","end":"2020-06-28","place":"Virtual","start":"2020-06-26","title":"ICSSP '20: Proceedings of the International Conference on Software and System Processes","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of St. Gallen"],"keyword":["Adaptive Case Management","Agile","Case study","Co creation","Declarative models","Local government","Prototyping","Regulatory compliance","Service Design","Traceability","Understandability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Syddjurs municipality"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ecoknow engineering effective co created and compliant adaptive case management systems for knowledge workers","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3379177.3388908","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-082.74-037184","identifier":[{"id":"85092529434","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cbaff1f9-829a-401c-88d1-79d34ba67628","ku-a11fcd9c-9dcc-4916-a4a7-2e012140fa90"],"keyword":["Adaptive case management","Agile","Case study","Co-creation","Declarative models","Local government","Prototyping","Regulatory compliance","Service design","Traceability","Understandability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-28FDD0983074960111B27426550C6C12"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3379177.3388908","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/215121089/ICSSP20_Ecoknow_overview.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/287763074/3379177.3388908.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, 