{"abstract":"We provide the first formal model for declarative choreographies, which is able to express general omega-regular liveness properties. We use the Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs notation for both choreographies and end-points. We define end-point projection as a restriction of DCR graphs and derive the condition for end-point projectability from the causal relationships of the graph. We illustrate the results with a running example of a Buyer-Seller-Shipper protocol. All the examples are available for simulation in the online DCR workbench at http://dcr.tools/forte19.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Slaats, Tijs","López, Hugo A.","Debois, Søren","Carbone, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382348"],"event":{"acronym":"FORTE","title":"International Conference on Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreographies","Declarative models","Liveness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"declarative choreographies and liveness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84259682/DeclarativeChoreographies_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382348","identifier":[{"id":"85067365596","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-486fbcd3-85c7-42d1-9a66-809e6ade54d9"],"keyword":["Choreographies","Declarative models","Liveness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-4192F8BEA87681AD39220F45040EF23B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84259682/DeclarativeChoreographies_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo A.","key":"lópezpau","last":"López","name":"López, Hugo A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-21759-4_8","eisbn":["9783030217594"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"129-147","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"FORTE 2019: Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems","title":"International Conference on Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067365596"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-486fbcd3-85c7-42d1-9a66-809e6ade54d9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Declarative Choreographies and Liveness","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382348","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) has substantially strengthened the requirements for data processing systems, requiring audits at scale. We show how and to what extent these audits can be automated. We contribute an analysis of which parts of the GDPR can be monitored, a formalisation of these parts in metric first-order temporal logic, and an application of the MonPoly system to automatically audit these parts. We validate our ideas on a case study using log data from industry, detecting actual violations. Altogether, we demonstrate both in theory and practice how to automate GDPR compliance checking.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kock, Emma Arfelt","Basin, David","Debois, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382534"],"event":{"acronym":"ESORICS","title":"European Symposium on Research in Computer Security"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich"],"keyword":["GDPR compliance checking","General Data Protection Regulation","automated audits","data processing systems","metric first order temporal logic"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monitoring the gdpr european symposium on research in computer security","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84814983/esorics19.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382534","identifier":[{"id":"85075611770","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-54a376f2-543c-407f-8145-3045db248b4f"],"keyword":["GDPR compliance checking","General Data Protection Regulation","automated audits","data processing systems","metric first-order temporal logic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8FAEF7776C075697A6C74A1E34A063BC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84814983/esorics19.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma Arfelt","key":"kockpau","last":"Kock","name":"Kock, Emma Arfelt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"basinpau","last":"Basin","name":"Basin, David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-29959-0_33","eisbn":["9783030299590"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"681-699","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"European Symposium on Research in Computer Security","title":"Computer Security – ESORICS 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075611770"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-54a376f2-543c-407f-8145-3045db248b4f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Monitoring the GDPR : European Symposium on Research in Computer Security","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382534","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Process mining algorithms fall in two classes: imperative miners output flow diagrams, showing all possible paths, whereas declarative miners output constraints, showing the rules governing a process. But given a log, how do we know which of the two to apply? Assuming that logs exhibiting a large degree of variability are more suited for declarative miners, we can attempt to answer this question by defining a suitable measure of the variability of the log. This paper reports on an exploratory study into the use of entropy measures as metrics of variability. We survey notions of entropy used, e.g. in physics; we propose variant notions likely more suitable for the field of process mining; we provide an implementation of every entropy notion discussed; and we report entropy measures for a collection of both synthetic and real-life logs. Finally, based on anecdotal indications of which logs are better suited for declarative/imperative mining, we identify the most promising measures for future studies. For estimating overall entropy, global block and k-nearest neighbour estimators of entropy appear most promising and excel at identifying noise in logs. For estimating entropy rate we identify Lempel–Ziv and certain variants of k-block estimators performing well, and note that the former is more stable, but sensitive to noise, while the latter is less stable, being sensitive to cut-off constraints determining block size.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Back, Christoffer Olling","Debois, Søren","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S02-097.65-038395"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Entropy","Faculty of Science","Hybrid models","Information theory","Knowledge work","Process Variability","Process flexibility","Process mining"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"entropy as a measure of log variability","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84223381/entropy_as_a_measure_of_log_variability_canonical.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-097.65-038395","identifier":[{"id":"85067672241","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-de23a365-b22d-4ceb-a1b7-5f3d4408fda2","ku-6138a205-8885-4e01-82f4-aa3595788ac6"],"keyword":["Entropy","Faculty of Science","Hybrid Models","Information Theory","Knowledge Work","Process Flexbility","Process Flexibility","Process Mining","Process Variability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CAF891BCD6A56D4447948C6526C96DB4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84223381/entropy_as_a_measure_of_log_variability_canonical.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer Olling","key":"backpau","last":"Back","locid":"0ce144c3-eaf9-43e2-8f2b-03d6e4212b6a","name":"Back, Christoffer Olling","orcid":"0000-0001-7998-7167","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s13740-019-00105-3","issn":["18612032","18612040"],"issn_org":["18612032"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal on Data Semantics","pages":"129-156","status":"p","title":"Journal on Data Semantics","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067672241"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-de23a365-b22d-4ceb-a1b7-5f3d4408fda2","ku-6138a205-8885-4e01-82f4-aa3595788ac6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Entropy as a Measure of Log Variability","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.65-038395","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We present a general transformation of general omission resilient distributed algorithms into byzantine fault ones. The transformation uses the guarantees of integrity and confidentiality provided by a trusted execution environment to implement a byzantine failure detector. Correct processes in a transformed algorithm will operate as if byzantine faulty processes have crashed or their messages were dropped. The transformation adds no additional messages between processes, except for a pre-compute step, and the increase in states of the algorithm is linearly bounded: it is a 1-round, n=f+1 translation, making no assumptions of determinism.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Madsen, Mads Frederik","Gaub, Mikkel","Kirkbro, Malthe Ettrup","Debois, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384684"],"event":{"acronym":"EDCC","title":"European Dependable Computing Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Byzantine faults","SGX","TEE","TPM","Translation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transforming byzantine faults using a trusted execution environment","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84670086/EDCC2019_paper_13.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384684","identifier":[{"id":"85075639506","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e7e97669-d3b3-40ba-892b-50df40f05180"],"keyword":["Byzantine faults","SGX","TEE","TPM","translation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0DF95BC3E3B9227706D3AEC9A6FA4150"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84670086/EDCC2019_paper_13.pdf","version":"Authors Final V