{"abstract":"Blockchain technology offers a sizable promise to rethink the way interorganizational business processes are managed because of its potential to realize execution without a central party serving as a single point of trust (and failure). To stimulate research on this promise and the limits thereof, in this article, we outline the challenges and opportunities of blockchain for business process management (BPM). We first reflect how blockchains could be used in the context of the established BPM lifecycle and second how they might become relevant beyond. We conclude our discourse with a summary of seven research directions for investigating the application of blockchain technology in the context of BPM.","author_count":38,"contributors":["Mendling, Jan","Weber, Ingo","Van Der Aalst, Wil","Brocke, Jan vom","Cabanillas, Cristina","Daniel, Florian","Debois, Soren","Di Ciccio, Claudio","Dumas, Marlon","Dustdar, Schahram","Gal, Avigdor","Garcia-Banuelos, Luciano","Governatori, Guido","Hull, T. Richard","La Rosa, Marcello","Leopold, Henrik","Leymann, Frank","Recker, Jan","Reichert, Manfred","Reijers, Hajo A.","Rinderle-Ma, Stefanie","Rogge-Solti, Andreas","Rosemann, Michael","Schulte, Stefan","Singh, Munindar P.","Slaats, Tijs","Staples, Mark","Weber, Barbara","Weidlich, Matthias","Weske, Mathias","Xu, Xiwei","Zhu, Liming"],"cuid":["S03-093.29-034474"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Estonia","Germany","Israel","Italy","Liechtenstein","Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Data 61 - Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation","Data61","Eindhoven University of Technology","Humboldt University of Berlin","IBM","IBM Research","North Carolina State University","Polytechnic University of Milan","Queens