ersity of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5365c1ed-09be-4923-87d6-83090f56c532","itu-33abdf41-c4d8-4bae-9852-d907caafe5cd","ku-0536375b-daad-458d-a47a-eedb03ee00e5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Blockchains for Business Process Management - Challenges and Opportunities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-093.29-034474","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The adoption of formal models by process specialists has faced two challenges: First, it requires process specialists to get training in formal modeling. Second, the resulting specifications bear little resemblance wrt. the original descriptions. We introduce a tool that supports translations between natural language descriptions and declarative process models. The resulting models are given in a graphical formalism, DCR Graphs. Traceability is at the core of the tool: Later changes in the process model due to, e.g., ambiguity resolution are traced back into the text. This allows users to either correct and complete their descriptions, or to derive models more refined than the text. In this paper, we describe the mechanics of the tool and provide examples of its use. Finally, we report on experiences using the tool in a Danish Municipal government.","author_count":4,"contributors":["López-Acosta, Hugo-Andrés","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Debois, Søren","Marquard, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382508"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Business process management","Digitalization","Law modelling","Process change","Process highlighter","Process models"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["DCR Solutions"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the process highlighter from texts to declarative processes and back","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85053597666","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382508","identifier":[{"id":"85053597666","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-52c168cc-b561-41bc-ac77-c941f4b30cca"],"keyword":["Business Process Management","Digitalization","Law modelling","Process Models","Process change","Process highlighter"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7C1B48D593EB8677D625B83103E0B29E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["DCR Solutions","Exformatics"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo-Andrés","key":"lópezacostapau","last":"López-Acosta","name":"López-Acosta, Hugo-Andrés","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"marquardpau","last":"Marquard","name":"Marquard, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779493704"],"issn":["16006100"],"issue":"TR-2018-204","pages":"19","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","repno":"IT University Technical Report Series, TR-2018-204","series":"IT University Technical Report Series","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-52c168cc-b561-41bc-ac77-c941f4b30cca"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Process Highlighter : From Texts to Declarative Processes and Back","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382508","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Rules, decisions, and workflows are intertwined components depicting the overall process. So far imperative workflow modelling languages have played the major role for the description and analysis of business processes. Despite their undoubted efficacy in representing sequential executions, they hide circumstantial information leading to the enactment of activities, and obscure the rationale behind the verification of requirements, dependencies, and goals. This workshop aimed at providing a platform for the discussion and introduction of new ideas related to the development of a holistic approach that encompasses all those aspects. The objective was to extend the reach of the business process management audience towards the decisions and rules community and increase the integration between different imperative, declarative and hybrid modelling perspectives. Out of the high-quality submitted manuscripts, three papers were accepted for publication, with an acceptance rate of 50%. They contributed to foster a fruitful discussion among the participants about the respective impact and the interplay of decision perspective and the process perspective.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Vanthienen, Jan","Di Ciccio, Claudio","Reijers, Hajo A.","Slaats, Tijs","Schunselaar, Dennis","Debois, Soren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434964"],"event":{"acronym":"BPM","end":"2017-09-15","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2017-09-10","title":"15th International Conference on Business Process Management","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Entropy","Hybrid models","Information theory","Knowledge work","Process mining","Process variability Process flexibility"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000005th international workshop on declarative decision hybrid mining and modeling for business processes dehmimop 000000000017","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-434964","ids":["ku-45972a8e-7928-4902-9531-11b67347a8a5"],"keyword":["Entropy","Hybrid models","Information theory","Knowledge Work","Process mining","Process variability Process flexibility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-56E900F0DD0EB800717305EB443D28A9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"vanthienenpau","last":"Vanthienen","name":"Vanthienen, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Claudio","key":"dicicciopau","last":"Di Ciccio","name":"Di Ciccio, Claudio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hajo A.","key":"reijerspau","last":"Reijers","name":"Reijers, Hajo A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dennis","key":"schunselaarpau","last":"Schunselaar","name":"Schunselaar, Dennis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Soren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Soren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ernest","key":"tenientepedh","last":"Teniente","name":"Teniente, Ernest","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"weidlichpedh","last":"Weidlich","name":"Weidlich, Matthias","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-74030-0_4","eisbn":["9783319740300"],"isbn":["9783319740294"],"pages":"526-541","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Business Information Processing","status":"p","subtitle":"BPM 2017 International Workshops, Barcelona, Spain, September 10–11, 2017, Revised Papers","title":"Business Process Management Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041726288"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-45972a8e-7928-4902-9531-11b67347a8a5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"5th International Workshop on Declarative/Decision/Hybrid Mining and Modeling for Business Processes (DeHMiMoP’17)","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-434964","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) gives primacy to purpose: Data may be collected and stored only when (i) end-users have consented, often explicitly, to the purposes for which that data is collected, and (ii) the collected data is actually necessary for achieving these purposes. This development in data protection regulations begets the question: how do we audit a computer system's adherence to a purpose? We propose an approach that identies a purpose with a business process, and show how formal models of interprocess communication can be used to audit or even derive privacy policies. Based on this insight, we propose a methodology for auditing GDPR compliance. Moreover, we show how given a simple interprocess data ow model, aspects of GDPR compliance can be determined algorithmically.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Basin, David","Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384602"],"event":{"acronym":"FC","title":"International Conference on Financial Cryptography and Data Security"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Business process modeling","Data Protection Regulation","GDPR Compliance","Interprocess Communication","Privacy Policy Auditing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on purpose and by necessity compliance under the gdpr","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84212312/On_Purpose_and_ny_Necessity.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384602","identifier":[{"id":"85072871760","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e23c4ee6-3ae8-4788-94a0-404cd4aa3518"],"keyword":["Business Process Modeling","Data Protection Regulation","GDPR Compliance","Interprocess Communication","Privacy Policy Auditing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EA673B61C6975B2B80BE49EC7E98139C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84212312/On_Purpose_and_ny_Necessity.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"basinpau","last":"Basin","name":"Basin, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783662583876"],"isbn":["9783662583869"],"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Financial Cryptography and Data Security. 22nd International Conference, FC 2018, Nieuwpoort, Curaçao, February 26 – March 2, 2018,"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072871760"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e23c4ee6-3ae8-4788-94a0-404cd4aa3518"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On Purpose and by Necessity: Compliance under the GDPR","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384602","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The adoption of formal models by process specialists has faced two challenges: First, it requires process specialists to get training in formal modeling. Second, the resulting specifications bear little resemblance wrt. the original descriptions. We introduce a tool that supports translations between natural language descriptions and declarative process models. The resulting models are given in a graphical formalism, DCR Graphs. Traceability is at the core of the tool: Later changes in the process model due to, eg, ambiguity resolution are traced back into the text. This allows users to either correct and complete their descriptions, or to derive models more refined than the text. In this paper, we describe the mechanics of the tool and provide examples of its use. Finally, we report on experiences using the tool in a Danish Municipal government.","author_count":4,"contributors":["López-Acosta, Hugo-Andrés","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Debois, Søren","Marquard, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384968"],"event":{"acronym":"BIR","title":"International Conference on Perspectives in Business Informatics Research"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Business process management","Digitalization","Process highlighter","Process models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["DCR Solutions"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the process highlighter from texts to declarative processes and back","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83415355/BPM_2018_paper_14.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384968","ids":["itu-fb4bfb79-5e72-492b-a7fc-67938633b7f3"],"keyword":["Business Process Management","Digitalization","Process Models","Process highlighter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3D8CCF536FFA7E753B35004E8D8F8B06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83415355/BPM_2018_paper_14.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2196/BPM_2018_paper_14.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["DCR Solutions"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo-Andrés","key":"lópezacostapau","last":"López-Acosta","name":"López-Acosta, Hugo-Andrés","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"marquardpau","last":"Marquard","name":"Marquard, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","pages":"66-70","publisher":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053597666"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fb4bfb79-5e72-492b-a7fc-67938633b7f3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Process Highlighter: From Texts to Declarative Processes and Back","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384968","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Process mining algorithms can be partitioned by the type of model that they output: imperative miners output flow-diagrams showing all possible paths through a process, whereas declarative miners output constraints showing the rules governing a process. For processes with great variability, the latter approach tends to provide better results, because using an imperative miner would lead to so-called “spaghetti models” which attempt to show all possible paths and are impossible to read. However, studies have shown that one size does not fit all: many processes contain both structured and unstructured parts and therefore do not fit strictly in one category or the other. This has led to the recent introduction of hybrid miners, which aim to combine flow- and constraint-based models to provide the best possible representation of a log. In this paper we focus on a core question underlying the development of hybrid miners: given a log, can we determine a priori whether the log is best suited for imperative or declarative mining? We propose using the concept of entropy, commonly used in information theory. We consider different measures for entropy that could be applied and show through experimentation on both synthetic and real-life logs that these entropy measures do indeed give insights into the complexity of the log and can act as an indicator of which mining paradigm should be used.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Back, Christoffer Olling","Debois, Soren","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471666"],"event":{"acronym":"BPM","end":"2017-09-15","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2017-09-10","title":"15th International Conference on Business Process Management","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Entropy","Hybrid models","Information theory","Knowledge work","Process mining","Process variability Process flexibility"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards an entropy based analysis of log variability","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/202483471/Back_2017_Towards_an_entropy_based.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471666","identifier":[{"id":"85041716336","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000434845200005","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-82be4502-fbc4-45b3-9d64-50274b0a3a07"],"keyword":["Entropy","Hybrid models","Information theory","Knowledge Work","Process mining","Process variability Process flexibility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-4A7658B8C053CF09D97A0D17B022CCA6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/202483471/Back_2017_Towards_an_entropy_based.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer Olling","key":"backpau","last":"Back","locid":"0ce144c3-eaf9-43e2-8f2b-03d6e4212b6a","name":"Back, Christoffer Olling","orcid":"0000-0001-7998-7167","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Soren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Soren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ernest","key":"tenientepedh","last":"Teniente","name":"Teniente, Ernest","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"weidlichpedh","last":"Weidlich","name":"Weidlich, Matthias","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-74030-0_4","eisbn":["9783319740300"],"isbn":["9783319740294"],"pages":"53-70","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Business Information Processing","status":"p","subtitle":"BPM 2017 International Workshops, Barcelona, Spain, September 10–11, 2017, Revised Papers","title":"Business Process Management Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041716336"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-82be4502-fbc4-45b3-9d64-50274b0a3a07"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards an Entropy-Based Analysis of Log Variability","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471666","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We introduce open tests to support iterative test-driven process modelling. Open tests generalise the trace-based tests of Zugal et al. to achieve modularity: whereas a trace-based test passes if a model exhibits a particular trace, an open test passes if a model exhibits a particular trace up to abstraction from additional activities not relevant for the test. This generalisation aligns open tests better with iterative test-driven development: open tests may survive the addition of activities and rules to the model in cases where trace-based tests do not. To reduce overhead in re-running tests, we establishing sufficient conditions for a model update to preserve test outcomes. We introduce open tests in an abstract setting that applies to any process notation with trace semantics, and give our main preservation result in this setting. Finally, we instantiate the general theory for the DCR Graph process notation, obtaining a method for iterative test-driven DCR process modelling.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Slaats, Tijs","Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas T."],"cuid":["S02-081.52-038369"],"event":{"acronym":"BPM","end":"2018-09-14","place":"Sydney, au","start":"2018-09-09","title":"16th International Conference on Business Process Management, BPM 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Abstraction","DCR Graphs","Declarative","Iterative Test Driven Development","Open Tests","Process modelling","Test driven modelling","Trace Semantics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"open to change a theory for iterative test driven modelling","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83757499/Tijs_Slaats_et_al._2018_Open_to_Change_A_Theory_for_Iterative_Test_Driven.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-081.52-038369","identifier":[{"id":"85053639624","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b896d17f-ef6d-41e8-9e9f-b84028fb5d1e","ku-0f35d0eb-7bc4-4030-ae95-334429d4f9c2"],"keyword":["Abstraction","DCR graphs","Declarative","Iterative Test-Driven Development","Open Tests","Process Modelling","Test-driven modelling","Trace Semantics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C1192ED484BDF5E29A870C35E4D60B4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83757499/Tijs_Slaats_et_al._2018_Open_to_Change_A_Theory_for_Iterative_Test_Driven.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","name_org":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marco","key":"montalipedh","last":"Montali","name":"Montali, Marco","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ingo","key":"weberpedh","last":"Weber","name":"Weber, Ingo","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mathias","key":"weskepedh","last":"Weske","name":"Weske, Mathias","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"vombrockepedh","last":"vom Brocke","name":"vom Brocke, Jan","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-98648-7_3","eisbn":["9783319986487"],"isbn":["9783319986470"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"31-47","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 16th International Conference on Business Process Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053639624"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b896d17f-ef6d-41e8-9e9f-b84028fb5d1e","ku-0f35d0eb-7bc4-4030-ae95-334429d4f9c2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Open to Change: A Theory for Iterative Test-Driven Modelling","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.52-038369","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We explore the complexity of reachability and run-time refinement under safety and liveness constraints in event-based process models. Our study is framed in the DCR? process language, which supports modular specification through a compositional operational semantics. DCR? encompasses the “Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs” declarative process model for analysis, execution and safe run-time refinement of process-aware information systems; including replication of sub-processes. We prove that event-reachability and refinement are np-hard for DCR? processes without replication, and that these finite state processes recognise exactly the languages that are the union of a regular and an ω-regular language. Moreover, we prove that eventreachability and refinement are undecidable in general for DCR? processes with replication and local events, and we provide a tractable approximation for refinement. A prototype implementation of the DCR ⋆ language is available at http://dcr.tools/acta16","author_count":3,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S02-092.11-038324"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Complexity","DCR Graphs","Refinement","Replication"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"replication refinement amp reachability complexity in dynamic condition response graphs","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346574961/dcrpl_AI.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-092.11-038324","identifier":[{"id":"85029696591","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-73adad41-a371-49c5-b50c-90e32dffd95f","ku-1de1ddf4-e71c-46dd-b65b-94ee35dd61f1"],"keyword":["DCR graphs","complexity","refinement","replication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F045EBCD5B68670AF3220D2B587ACC4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442966/dcrpl_AI.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346574961/dcrpl_AI.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00236-017-0303-8","issn":["00015903","14320525"],"issn_org":["00015903"],"journal":"Acta Informatica","pages":"1-32","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Acta Informatica"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029696591"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-73adad41-a371-49c5-b50c-90e32dffd95f","ku-1de1ddf4-e71c-46dd-b65b-94ee35dd61f1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Replication, refinement &amp; reachability : complexity in dynamic condition-response graphs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.11-038324","year":2018,"yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"We investigate process mining for the declarative Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs process modelling language. We contribute (a) a process mining algorithm for DCR graphs, (b) a proposal for a set of metrics quantifying output model quality, and (c) a preliminary example-based comparison with the Declare Maps Miner. The algorithm takes a contradiction-based approach, that is, we initially assume that all possible constraints hold, subsequently removing constraints as they are observed to be violated by traces in the input log.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Laursen, Paw Høvsgaard","Ulrik, Kenneth Ry"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381386"],"event":{"acronym":"SAC","title":"ACM Symposium on Applied Computing"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DCR graphs declarative process mining"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"declarative process mining for dcr graphs","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83000958/p759_debois.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381386","identifier":[{"id":"85020855546","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-089a2087-8146-4cef-9581-8c41d9b8e227"],"keyword":["DCR graphs, declarative process mining"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FFD2FF880F223632EA78D66117BBA902"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83000958/p759_debois.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Paw Høvsgaard","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","name":"Laursen, Paw Høvsgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth Ry","key":"ulrikpau","last":"Ulrik","name":"Ulrik, Kenneth Ry","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3019612.3019622","isbn":["9781450344869"],"pages":"759-764","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"SAC '17","title":"Proceedings of the Symposium on Applied Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020855546"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-089a2087-8146-4cef-9581-8c41d9b8e227"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Declarative Process Mining for DCR Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381386","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Digitalisation of work and business processes with the aim to provide more efficient services at a higher and consistent quality is high on the agendas in many countries. In Denmark the push for digitalisation is witnessed by the national strategy for digitalisation published every four years. Sadly, it is also witnessed by a number of expensive failed digitalisation projects. In this paper we point to two key problems in state-of-The art BPM technologies: 1) the use of rigid flow diagrams as the \"source code\" of process digitalisation is not suitable for managing the complexity of knowledge workflows and regulations and 2) insufficient support for continuous and agile end-user mapping and adaptation of processes. We report on research in progress on how the Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) Graph technology and collaborative process repository DCRGraphs.net could support agile and collaborative, bottom-up digitalisation of business and workflow processes.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas","Debois, Søren","Slaats, Tijs","Marquard, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-538354"],"event":{"end":"2017-08-30","place":"København, dk","start":"2017-08-28","title":"2nd Workshop on Managed Complexity","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"managing complexity in process digitalisation with dynamic condition response graphs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85029151827&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-538354","identifier":[{"id":"8