{"abstract":"We report on experiences from a case study applying a constraint-based process-modelling and -simulation tool, dcrgraphs.net, to the modelling and rehearsal of railway emergency response plans with domain experts. The case study confirmed the approach as a viable means for domain experts to analyse and rehearse emergency response plans, through the activities of formally modelling the plan and subsequently rehearsing it by simulating that model collaboratively. In particular, the constraint-based modelling notation resulted in a flexible model giving rehearsal participants freedom to explore different ways to proceed, including ways not necessarily anticipated in the paper-based emergency response plans. The case study was undertaken as part of a short research, ProSec, project funded by the Danish Defence Agency, with the aim of applying and developing methods for collaborative mapping of emergency and security processes in the danish public transport sector and their dependency on ICT.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Sandberg, Lene"],"cuid":["S02-095.65-038400"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Case studies","Collaborative Rehearsal","Constraint based Process Modelling","Cooperative learning","Emergency management","It","Railway Emergency Response","Security Processes in Public Transport","Simulation tool"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experience report constraint based modelling and simulation of railway emergency response plans","src":["itu","kp"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procs.2016.04.269","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.65-038400","identifier":[{"id":"84971320579","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e12ad2f8-60b2-4d15-b01a-6c3196c9d80b","kp-342b27c1-ee02-437b-beb1-98ea2d46e847"],"keyword":["Collaborative Rehearsal","Constraint-based Process Modelling","Railway Emergency Response","Security Processes in Public Transport","Simulation Tool","case studies","cooperative learning","emergency management","it"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-77AD31C82C7E418FE30745D7148EA1EA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82367853/1_s2.0_S1877050916303027_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procs.2016.04.269","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for pædagogiske og samfundsfaglige uddannelser-Dekan, Katastrofe- og Risikomanageruddannelsen","Societal safety and security"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"sandbergpau","last":"Sandberg","locid":"45607bcd-7c3b-49ea-8b5d-a006ee44133e","name":"Sandberg, Lene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.procs.2016.04.269","issn":["18770509"],"journal":"Procedia Computer Science","pages":"1295-1300","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Procedia Computer Science","volume":"83"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84971320579"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","KP","Universities","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e12ad2f8-60b2-4d15-b01a-6c3196c9d80b","kp-342b27c1-ee02-437b-beb1-98ea2d46e847"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Experience Report: Constraint-Based Modelling and Simulation of Railway Emergency Response Plans","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.65-038400","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Case Management (CM) is a BPM technology for supporting flexible services orchestration. CM approaches like CMMN, an OMG standard, and GSM, one of CMMN’s core influences, use Event- Condition-Action rules, which can be inconsistent due to cyclic interdependencies between the rules; repairing such an inconsistent case management schema is difficult. To avoid the problem of inconsistencies altogether, we provide a technique for automatically deriving consistent GSM case management schemas from higher-level business policies defined as DCR graphs, an alternative CM approach. Concretely, we define a behaviour-preserving mapping that (1) removes the burden from the modeller of GSM schemas to prove consistency and define the ordering of rules, (2) provides high-level patterns for modelling GSM schemas, and (3) gives a way to define a notion of progress (liveness) and acceptance for GSM instances. The mapping is illustrated by a running example of a mortgage loan application; and a prototype implementation available at http://dcr.itu.dk/icsoc16.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Eshuis, Rik","Debois, Søren","Slaats, Tijs","Hildebrandt, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-081.59-038268"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSOC","end":"2016-10-13","place":"Banff, ca","start":"2016-10-10","title":"14th International Conference on Service-Oriented Computing","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology"],"keyword":["Business Process Management BPM","Case Management","DCR Graphs","Event Condition Action ECA rules","GSM schemas"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deriving consistent gsm schemas from dcr graphs","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82357496/EshuisDeboisSlaatsHildebrandt_ICSOC.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-081.59-038268","identifier":[{"id":"84989298051","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1e9f566e-e736-4005-93ca-d319ba01b0bb","ku-ecbf19b1-7490-4716-af46-ec84a796e4af"],"keyword":["Business Process Management (BPM)","Case Management","DCR graphs","Event-Condition-Action (ECA) rules","GSM schemas"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2A87FF74D7EE61C9CABDD300C4700457"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82357496/EshuisDeboisSlaatsHildebrandt_ICSOC.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rik","key":"eshuispau","last":"Eshuis","name":"Eshuis, Rik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Quan Z.","key":"shengpedh","last":"Sheng","name":"Sheng, Quan Z.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eleni","key":"strouliapedh","last":"Stroulia","name":"Stroulia, Eleni","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Samir","key":"tatapedh","last":"Tata","name":"Tata, Samir","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sami","key":"bhiripedh","last":"Bhiri","name":"Bhiri, Sami","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-46295-0_29","eisbn":["9783319462950"],"isbn":["9783319462943"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"467-482","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"14th International Conference, ICSOC 2016, Banff, AB, Canada, October 10-13, 2016, Proceedings","title":"Service-oriented computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84989298051"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","exformatics a/s (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1e9f566e-e736-4005-93ca-d319ba01b0bb","ku-ecbf19b1-7490-4716-af46-ec84a796e4af"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deriving Consistent GSM Schemas from DCR Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.59-038268","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Danish mortgage credit institutes deal with highly variable and knowledgeintensive processes. At the same time these processes are required to be strictly conformant to current regulations and laws. In addition different divisions of the business are interested in different views on the same process: whereas the IT department implementing the processes would like a complete view that shows the underlying business rules and supports all variants, the end users are only interested in a local view that (1) shows only the aspects of the process that they are responsible for and (2) only shows the variants of the process that are relevant to them. This paper reports on a project we undertook with such a credit institute where we investigated and addressed these issues by providing a hybrid solution, allowing processes to be modelled using our constraint-based modelling tools, but also supporting flow-based views of both the entire process and specific variants.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Marquard, Morten","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383673"],"event":{"acronym":"BPM","title":"International Conference on Business Process Management"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Constraint based and flow based views","Danish mortgage credit institutes","Knowledge intensive processes","Process modeling","Regulatory compliance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hybrid process technologies in the financial sector","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1439/paper9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383673","ids":["itu-a4c0f936-2be7-440d-90f2-60b9333b654f"],"keyword":["- Constraint-based and flow-based views","- Danish mortgage credit institutes","- Knowledge-intensive processes","- Process modeling","- Regulatory compliance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-313E66D04E530DF046668DA3B0B61F37"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1439/paper9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828561/main_BPM2015_case.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"marquardpau","last":"Marquard","name":"Marquard, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"pages":"107-119","publisher":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","series":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the Industry Track at the 13th International Conference on Business Process Management 2015 (BPM-Industry 2015)","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","volume":"1439"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a4c0f936-2be7-440d-90f2-60b9333b654f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hybrid process technologies in the financial sector","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383673","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We study modularity, run-time adaptation and refinement under safety and liveness constraints in event-based process models with dynamic sub-process instantiation. The study is part of a larger programme to provide semantically well-founded technologies for modelling, implementation and verification of flexible, run-time adaptable process-aware information systems, moved into practice via the Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) Graphs notation co-developed with our industrial partner. Our key contributions are: (1) A formal theory of dynamic sub-process instantiation for declarative, event-based processes under safety and liveness constraints, given as the DCR* process language, equipped with a compositional operational semantics and conservatively extending the DCR Graphs notation; (2) an expressiveness analysis revealing that the DCR* process language is Turing-complete, while the fragment cor- responding to DCR Graphs (without dynamic sub-process instantiation) characterises exactly the languages that are the union of a regular and an omega-regular language; (3) a formalisation of run-time refinement and adaptation by composition for DCR* processes and a proof that such refinement is undecidable in general; and finally (4) a decidable and practically useful sub-class of run-time refinements. Our results are illustrated by a running example inspired by a recent Electronic Case Management solution based on DCR Graphs and delivered by our industrial partner. An online prototype implementation of the DCR* language (including examples from the paper) and its visualisation as DCR Graphs can be found at http://tiger.itu.dk:8018/.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383864"],"event":{"acronym":"FM","end":"2015-06-26","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2015-06-22","title":"The 20th International Symposium on Formal Methods","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Compositional Operational Semantics","DCR Graphs","Dynamic Sub process Instantiation","Event based Process Models","Modularity","Process aware Information Systems","Run time Adaptation","Run time Refinement and Adaptation","Safety and Liveness Constraints","Turing complete"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safety liveness and run time refinement for modular process aware information systems with dynamic sub processes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828583/dcrstar_full.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383864","identifier":[{"id":"84937510358","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b2083407-6f09-48cf-9111-770ab4dc2989"],"keyword":["- Compositional Operational Semantics","- DCR Graphs","- Dynamic Sub-process Instantiation","- Event-based Process Models","- Modularity","- Process-aware Information Systems","- Run-time Adaptation","- Run-time Refinement and Adaptation","- Safety and Liveness Constraints","- Turing-complete"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-262EAC13E96CDF2C9C58DC682C72AF8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828583/dcrstar_full.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nikolaj","key":"bjørnerpedh","last":"Bjørner","name":"Bjørner, Nikolaj","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Frank","key":"deboerpedh","last":"de Boer","name":"de Boer, Frank","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-19249-9_10","eisbn":["9783319192499"],"isbn":["9783319192482"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"143-160","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"20th International Symposium, Oslo, Norway, June 24-26, 2015, Proceedings","title":"FM 2015: Formal Methods"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84937510358"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b2083407-6f09-48cf-9111-770ab4dc2989"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Safety, Liveness and Run-time Refinement for Modular Process-Aware Information Systems with Dynamic Sub Processes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383864","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Declarative or constraint-based business process and workflow notations have received increasing interest in the last decade as possible means of addressing the challenge of supporting at the same time flexibility in execution, adaptability and compliance. However, the definition of concurrent semantics, which is a necessary foundation for asynchronously executing distributed processes, is not obvious for declarative formalisms and is so far virtually unexplored. This is in stark contrast to the very successful Petri-net–based process languages, which have an inherent notion of concurrency. In this paper, we pro- pose a notion of concurrency for declarative process models, formulated in the context of Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs, and exploiting the so-called “true concurrency” semantics of Labelled Asynchronous Transition Systems. We demonstrate how this semantic underpinning of concurrency in DCR Graphs admits asynchronous execution of declarative workflows both conceptually and by reporting on a prototype implementation of a distributed declarative workflow engine. Both the theoretical development and the implementation is supported by an extended example; moreover, the theoretical development has been verified correct in the Isabelle-HOL interactive theorem prover.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383470"],"event":{"acronym":"BPM","title":"International Conference on Business Process Management"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Asynchronous Execution","Concurrent Semantics","Declarative process models","Dynamic Condition Response DCR Graphs","Labelled Asynchronous Transition Systems LATS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"concurrency amp asynchrony in declarative workflows","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828530/Concurrency_and_Asynchrony.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383470","identifier":[{"id":"84944679867","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-964530cf-4e61-4d79-b720-12b3bdcd3685"],"keyword":["Asynchronous Execution","Concurrent Semantics","Declarative Process Models","Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) Graphs","Labelled Asynchronous Transition Systems (LATS)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0C45CACF9B3F89096C882D8DF70DAC72"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828528/Concurrency_and_Asynchrony_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828530/Concurrency_and_Asynchrony.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-23063-4_5","eisbn":["9783319230627"],"isbn":["9783319230627"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"72-89","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of 13th International Conference on Business Process Management (BPM 2015)","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"9253"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944679867"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-964530cf-4e61-4d79-b720-12b3bdcd3685"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Concurrency &amp; Asynchrony in Declarative Workflows","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383470","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Marquard, Morten","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384188"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSE","title":"International Conference on Software Engineering"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bridging the valley of death a success story on danish funding schemes paving a path from technology readiness level 000000000001 to 000000000009","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=2821401","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384188","identifier":[{"id":"84962310082","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c715a99b-7a8e-41ca-bafc-e9eb81c88b8b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C80820AA9C280EF7CBEB379A753D8ABC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"marquardpau","last":"Marquard","name":"Marquard, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781467370851"],"isbn":["9781467370851"],"pages":"54-57","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2nd International Workshop on Software Engineering Research and Industrial Practice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84962310082"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c715a99b-7a8e-41ca-bafc-e9eb81c88b8b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bridging the Valley of Death : A Success Story on Danish Funding Schemes Paving a Path from Technology Readiness Level 1 to 9","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384188","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This paper reports on a qualitative study of the use of declarative process notations used in a commercial setting. Specifically, we investigate the actual use of a system implemented in terms of DCR graphs for the Danish \"Dreyer Foundation\" by our industry partner Exformatics A/S. The study is performed by analysing logs of actual use of the system. By the study we seek to illuminate the currently open -- and heavily debated! -- research question of whether the claimed advantages in conciseness and flexibility of declarative models over more traditional flow-based notations are significant in practice. Studies investigating this question have typically focused on understandability for users, driven by lab experiments and workshops with practitioners unfamiliar with the paradigm. In the present study, we (1) attempt to assess qualitatively whether users employed the flexibility granted them by the declarative model, and (2) use process discovery techniques to examine if a perfect-fitness flow-based model representing the main business constraints is in fact easy to come by. For (1), we find evidence in various forms, most notably an apparent change in best practices by end-users allowed by the model. For (2), we find no such model. We leave as a challenge to the community the construction of a flow-based model adequately representing the business constraints and supporting all observed behaviour by the users, whether by hand or by mining.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Debois, Søren","Slaats, Tijs"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381506"],"event":{"acronym":"IEEE SSCI","end":"2015-12-10","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2015-12-07","title":"2015 IEEE Symposium on Computational Intelligence and Data Mining","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DCR Graphs","Declarative Process Notations","Flow based Models","Process discovery","Qualitative analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the analysis of a real life declarative process","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84964937353","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381506","identifier":[{"id":"84964937353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-100809a9-ede0-4351-9f40-944630fa99da"],"keyword":["DCR Graphs","Declarative Process Notations","Flow-based Models","Process Discovery","Qualitative Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-00AF3FF798771012E0FAC0FD83CB61B5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ssci.2015.196","isbn":["9781479975600"],"pages":"1374-1382","place":"IEEE","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2015 Symposium on Computational Intelligence and Data Mining (CIDM)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964937353"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-100809a9-ede0-4351-9f40-944630fa99da"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Analysis of a Real Life Declarative Process","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381506","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
